00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:34.919
Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for the solution.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:48.179
In general finding the prime factorization of a large number is a computationally difficult problem.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:52.380
So we're going to solve the problem using elementary number theory.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:02:01.020
The number N is the least common multiple, or LCM, of all the whole numbers from 1 to 100.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:07.720
So N is the product of the highest power of the primes from 1 to 100.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:11.960
This ensures that every single number from 1 to 100,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.580
whatever its prime factorization is, all of those prime factors will be included in N.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:23.669
So we include every prime number that's less than 100.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:30.120
We also need to account if there are repeated prime factors.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:35.790
In order to do that we find the highest power of each prime that's less than 100.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:43.530
For example: 2 to the 6th is equal to 64, so we need 6 factors of 2 in N.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:49.050
Now one more factor of 2, 2 to the seventh, would actually be larger than 100.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.709
It would be 128 so we do not have 7 factors of 2.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:03:01.500
Then we have 3 to the power of 4, is equal to 81, the next higher power would be higher than 100.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:05.070
We have 5 squared is equal to 25.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:12.149
7 squared is equal to 49, and then the next prime 11 square is larger than 100.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:15.929
So we don't have two factors of 11.

00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:24.929
Every other prime that's larger than 11 will have a square that exceeds 102, so we're done checking for repeated prime factors.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.039
So these are all the prime factors that are in N.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:38.080
So we can then write N is equal to the product of all these prime factors raised to the highest power that's less than 100.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.860
That's 2 to the power 6, 3 to the power 4, 5 squared, 7 squared

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:48.989
and then all the other primes,11, 13, 17, 19, 23, 29, 31, 37, 41

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:57.780
43, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89, and 97

